{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"GnustoTestSupport","externalID":"GnustoTestSupport","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GnustoTestSupport"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is a value and a play session is a function of its typed input, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the natural test is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"transcript test","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" boots"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns everything printed with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input interleaved as "},{"code":"> command","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the same text the player saw. Everything else"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in this library either cuts that string down to the part a claim is about, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records a Swift Testing issue with the whole of it attached, which is what a bare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"#expect(transcript.contains(…))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot do. Gnusto’s own suite is roughly a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thousand tests of this shape."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is neither a "},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle nor a "},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It declares no verbs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no rules and no entities, and a game never links it: it is a test-only helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, and it imports the toolchain’s Testing library, which ships with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler rather than the OS. Put it in a test target’s dependencies and nowhere"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else — an executable that links it can fail at load time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host passes a game type and a list of commands; the library holds one piece"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of state of its own, a process-wide cache of prepared games behind a "},{"code":"Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" exists because "},{"code":"Bootstrap.build","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reflects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over the game and every content bundle it lists, and that runs about 15× longer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a turn does. The suite boots the same handful of game types thousands of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times, so building each once and copying the prepared definition takes bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out of the suite’s critical path. "},{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" goes through it; a test that wants the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world rather than the transcript can call it directly and drive "},{"code":"REPL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gnusto catalog’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Testing Your Game","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" article teaches four of these helpers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the habits around them — pinning a seed, sweeping "},{"code":"GNUSTO_SEED","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that pass by luck, deciding when a trap is worth a test at all. This page is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it stops short of."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-transcript-test","type":"heading","text":"A transcript test","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","@Test func ringingTheBellWinsTheGame() async throws {","    let transcript = try await play(","        MyGame(),","        [\"take rope\", \"north\", \"ring bell\"],","        seed: 7)","","    expectInOrder(","        transcript,","        [","            \"Village Garden\",","            \"Taken.\",","            \"Bell Tower\",","            \"The great bronze bell peals\",","        ])","","    let looking = turnOutput(of: \"examine hook\", in: transcript)","    #expect(looking.contains(\"screwed to the wall\"))","    #expect(occurrences(of: \"The bell tolls\", in: transcript) == 1)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Omit "},{"code":"seed:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the stream is fresh each run, unless "},{"code":"GNUSTO_SEED","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pins every call that passed no seed of its own and leaves the ones that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"did alone. Pass "},{"code":"saveDirectory:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when a test exercises named "},{"code":"save","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it never writes to the real per-user saves directory."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Slicing-before-asserting","type":"heading","text":"Slicing before asserting","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"turnOutput(of:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" matches the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" occurrence of a command, so a route"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that types "},{"code":"look","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" four times wants four different commands or a different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"helper. "},{"code":"output(after:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"output(before:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cut on any marker rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a prompt, which is the slice for “and then, later…”. "},{"code":"occurrences(of:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the count assertion — a beat that must fire exactly once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"lines(mentioning:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the matching lines in transcript order, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what an alignment check compares between two runs to prove that a guard burned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no randomness."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Asserting","type":"heading","text":"Asserting","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"expectInOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the workhorse: a sequence of substrings, each match resuming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the last, strict enough to pin the beats that matter and loose enough to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"survive an edit between them. The rest of the assertions are about a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript rather than a phrase in it. "},{"code":"expectEveryNounAnswered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer a game gives a noun it doesn’t know — "},{"code":"I don't know the word \"x\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"You can't see any such thing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is what a walk of "},{"code":"x <noun>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room’s own description is checking. "},{"code":"expectNoAmbiguity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Which do you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mean…","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", and is deliberately a separate call: an unanswered noun is always a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defect, while an ambiguity is only one where the author believed the room held a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single thing of that kind."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for a game that has re-voiced the stub verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and wants to keep the claim whole. It reads "},{"code":"text.stubs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than naming the properties, so a stub added to the engine tomorrow is compared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the day it lands. "},{"code":"engineVoicedStubLines","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same sweep without the issue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recording, split out so the sweep itself can be tested for being alive — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection loop that matches nothing passes silently."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","type":"heading","text":"Trapping a `fatalError`","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine answers an authoring mistake by crashing with a message that names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. A "},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it in a child process and read what it printed; Swift Testing’s exit tests do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the running and "},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does the reading."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(MyGame(), [\"prime the bomb\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"names a daemon\", \"use startDaemon(_:)\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call is a child process, some 60 ms against 1 ms for an in-process"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assertion, and the "},{"code":"#expect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has to stay at the call site because its body is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiled into a C function that captures nothing. "},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own doc comment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carries the rule for when that is worth spending, since it is where the person"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deciding is standing: make the bad message unrepresentable and write no test,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or split the message into a pure function and assert it in a millisecond, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaching for the third shape. Exit tests are built on macOS, Linux and Windows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and are absent elsewhere, so "},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is compiled under "},{"code":"GNUSTO_EXIT_TESTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a test using it wants a "},{"code":"#if","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a suite that also runs on iOS, watchOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tvOS, visionOS or WASI."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"],"title":"Playing a session","anchor":"Playing-a-session"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(after:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)"],"title":"Slicing a transcript","anchor":"Slicing-a-transcript"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"],"title":"Asserting","anchor":"Asserting"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"],"title":"Trapping a `fatalError`","anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/frame(headed:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(ofLast:in:)"],"title":"Functions","anchor":"Functions","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expectNoAmbiguity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","text":"SourceLocation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a Swift Testing issue if the transcript contains a disambiguation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"question — "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Which do you mean: the narrow chimney or the small door?”"}],"type":"emphasis"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expectnoambiguity(_:_:sourcelocation:)","title":"expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/lines(mentioning:in:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"lines(mentioning:in:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)","abstract":[{"text":"The lines of a transcript slice that mention ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"needle"},{"text":", in order.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lines","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"mentioning","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/stockFragment(of:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stockFragment","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9StockLineP","text":"StockLine","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"stockFragment(of:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/stockfragment(of:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part of a stock line no subject can vary — the engine’s own wording,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the noun taken out."}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV11StubRepliesV","text":"StubReplies","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"game","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"sourceLocation","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","text":"SourceLocation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","abstract":[{"text":"Records a Swift Testing issue for every stub-verb line a game still answers","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the engine’s voice."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expectnoenginestublinesurvives(in:game:sourcelocation:)","title":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/output(before:in:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"output","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"before","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"type":"topic","title":"output(before:in:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/output(before:in:)","abstract":[{"text":"Everything a transcript printed before its first occurrence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"marker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectNoStockRefusal"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"text":", [any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9StockLineP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StockLine"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sourceLocation","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","text":"SourceLocation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expectnostockrefusal(_:_:_:sourcelocation:)","abstract":[{"text":"Records a Swift Testing issue for every engine stock line that survives in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"transcript."}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/turnOutput(of:in:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"turnOutput(of:in:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/turnoutput(of:in:)","abstract":[{"text":"The output of a single command within a transcript: everything between","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> command"},{"type":"text","text":" line and the next prompt (or the end). Returns"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"“” when the command never appears."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"turnOutput"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expectTrap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExitTest","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing8ExitTestV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing